##! experimental.virtual_source experimental.persistence experimental.join_types experimental.givens experimental.access_modifiers
import "../index.malloy"
import "./shared_queries.malloy"

// "Tell it what you like" — the INPUT half of the fork, split out of next_watch
// on 2026-08-07 (NEXT-LAYOUT-WORK.md §3, Andrew's heaviest-weighted item:
// "instead of making one page that is crowded and has every tool jammed in,
// let's make different pages for different tools").
//
// This page's ONE job is collecting verdicts. `next_watch` reads them back and
// its one job is the output. They share the visitor's profile through
// `dashboards/lib/profile.js` (localStorage) and through the URL givens, so
// there is no server and no new plumbing between them.
//
// ⛑ THE GIVENS BELOW ARE DECLARED HERE, NOT IMPORTED. Malloy's `import` does not
// re-export another dashboard's `given:` block, and a dashboard artifact can only
// bind givens declared in its own model. They intentionally mirror next_watch's
// so a link carrying ratings works in either direction.

given:
  # label="Year"
  RELEASE_YEAR :: filter<number> is f''

// ── the rating pool ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The artifact is the SHARED `seed_titles` (./shared_queries.malloy), not a copy.
// A first draft of this page defined its own `rate_seed` with the same shape;
// that is exactly the duplication the split is supposed to avoid, so it was
// deleted once the import mechanism was proven to work.
# artifact { title="Rate what you've seen" givens { GENRE="" RELEASE_YEAR="" } }
# dashboard
#" Well-known films to react to
query: rate_page is seed_titles
